    {
      "slug":"arugambay",
      "short_description":"A storied east-coast surf town where point breaks, lagoons and unhurried beach life meet the edge of the wild.",
      "full_description":"Arugam Bay is best known for the long, clean lines of its main point break, yet the place reveals more when explored beyond the surf. Sandy lanes lead to cafés and small guesthouses, fishing boats return at first light, and nearby lagoons and dry-zone landscapes bring wildlife remarkably close to the coast. The mood is sociable but relaxed, with sunrise sessions and slow evenings setting the rhythm.",
      "why_visit":"Come for world-class surf conditions, stay for the east coast’s easy pace and the contrast between ocean, lagoon and dry-zone wilderness.",
      "historical_importance":null,
      "cultural_significance":"The bay remains connected to Muslim and Tamil coastal communities, fishing traditions and the sacred landscapes around nearby Muhudu Maha Viharaya and Okanda. Respectful dress is appreciated away from the beach.",
      "unesco_information":null,
      "nature_wildlife":"Lagoons and scrubland around Pottuvil support elephants, crocodiles, water birds and monkeys. Wildlife encounters should be made with licensed, low-impact operators and generous distance.",
      "best_time_to_visit":"May to September usually offers the most reliable surf and driest east-coast weather. November to February is quieter and wetter, with some seasonal businesses reducing hours.",
      "weather":"Warm year-round, commonly 27–33°C. The east coast is generally driest from May to September, while the northeast monsoon brings more rain and occasional rough seas from November into February.",
      "local_highlights":["Sunrise surf at Main Point and nearby breaks","Lagoon safaris through quiet bird habitat","Fishing-village mornings and relaxed beach evenings","Elephant Rock viewpoints and coastal walks","A day journey towards Kumana’s wetlands"],
      "nearby_attractions":["Pottuvil Lagoon","Muhudu Maha Viharaya","Elephant Rock","Kumana National Park","Okanda coastal sanctuary"],
      "travel_tips":["Match surf breaks to your ability and use an experienced local instructor.","Carry cash because smaller businesses may not accept cards.","Keep a respectful distance from elephants seen outside protected areas.","Plan transfers in advance; the east-coast journey is long but rewarding."]
    },
    {
      "slug":"balapitiya",
      "short_description":"A southern river town opening onto the Madu Ganga’s mangroves, islands and quietly cinematic waterways.",
      "full_description":"Balapitiya is the gateway to one of the south coast’s most absorbing wetland landscapes. The Madu Ganga threads between mangrove banks, cinnamon-growing islands and small waterside communities before meeting the sea. It is a place for an early boat journey, patient birdwatching and a closer view of how river and coastal life overlap.",
      "why_visit":"Choose Balapitiya for a softer adventure: intimate waterways, village stories and nature close to the established southern-coast route.",
      "historical_importance":null,
      "cultural_significance":"River islands support long-standing fishing, cinnamon and Buddhist traditions. The best visits favour community knowledge and avoid staged wildlife handling.",
      "unesco_information":null,
      "nature_wildlife":"The Madu Ganga wetland includes mangroves, mudflats and islands used by water birds, reptiles and aquatic life. Its value lies in the complete estuarine system rather than any single sighting.",
      "best_time_to_visit":"December to April often brings brighter, calmer conditions. Early morning is rewarding throughout the year, with fewer boats and better wildlife activity.",
      "weather":"Tropical and humid, usually 26–31°C. Rain is possible year-round, with wetter spells during the southwest monsoon and the inter-monsoon months.",
      "local_highlights":["A quiet morning boat journey on the Madu Ganga","Mangrove channels and island scenery","Traditional cinnamon cultivation","Water birds along the estuary","A slow transition between river and coast"],
      "nearby_attractions":["Ahungalla","Ambalangoda","Kosgoda","Bentota","Hikkaduwa"],
      "travel_tips":["Choose a licensed operator who avoids feeding or handling wildlife.","Travel early for cooler temperatures and quieter waterways.","Carry insect protection and a light rain layer.","Ask before photographing residents on the smaller islands."]
    },
    {
      "slug":"bentota",
      "short_description":"A polished southwest-coast escape pairing a broad golden beach with river adventures, gardens and refined stays.",
      "full_description":"Bentota balances beach time with a surprising variety of experiences. The wide shore invites long walks and restful days, while the Bentota River offers watersports and gentler journeys through palm-lined channels. Elegant architecture, landscaped gardens and easy rail access give the area a composed character that works especially well at the beginning or end of an island itinerary.",
      "why_visit":"Visit for an effortless coastal stay with enough river, design and cultural interest to make every day feel different.",
      "historical_importance":null,
      "cultural_significance":"Bentota’s modern identity is closely linked to Sri Lankan tropical modernism, especially the work and gardens associated with Geoffrey and Bevis Bawa in the surrounding area.",
      "unesco_information":null,
      "nature_wildlife":"Riverbanks, wetlands and the nearby Madu Ganga support birds and estuarine life. Sea-turtle conservation projects operate along the wider coast and should be selected for responsible practices.",
      "best_time_to_visit":"December to April is usually best for calmer seas and sunnier beach days. River experiences remain possible for much of the year, adjusted around rainfall.",
      "weather":"Warm and humid, generally 26–31°C. The southwest monsoon is most influential from May to September, with additional showers often around October and November.",
      "local_highlights":["Long golden-beach walks","Bentota River adventures and sunset cruises","Lunuganga’s landscape and design legacy","Brief Garden near Beruwala","Thoughtful resort stays with easy Colombo access"],
