      "full_description":"Kalpitiya feels elemental: steady wind over the lagoon, fishing boats on the horizon and narrow strips of land between sea and water. Kitesurfers are drawn by the seasonal conditions, while offshore excursions reveal dolphins and the wider marine landscape. The peninsula remains working and local, rewarding travellers who value activity over polish.",
      "why_visit":"Come for Sri Lanka’s leading kitesurfing environment and a remote coastal character that feels distinct from the southern beach circuit.",
      "historical_importance":"Kalpitiya’s position on old maritime routes is reflected in its colonial-era Dutch Fort and the layered trading history of the peninsula.",
      "cultural_significance":"Fishing communities, churches, mosques and coastal villages give the peninsula a diverse identity. Tourism works best when it supports local operators and respects working shorelines.",
